1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,781
October 18, 1958. Long Island, New York.

2
00:00:05,961 --> 00:00:13,659
A physicist who worked on the atomic bomb has a much smaller problem: visitors to his laboratory are getting bored.

3
00:00:13,959 --> 00:00:19,771
So he connects a computer to a five-inch screen… and draws a ball.

4
00:00:19,951 --> 00:00:22,441
Massive lines begin to form.

5
00:00:23,091 --> 00:00:24,978
He never patents it.

6
00:00:25,978 --> 00:00:32,846
Sixty-eight years later, that dot of light moves more than $200 billion a year.

7
00:00:33,026 --> 00:00:36,799
And the entire world is counting down the days for a single game.

8
00:00:37,249 --> 00:00:40,117
This is the history of video games.
